{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-5bc453c9ca0524062154","statement":"If $P \\subset \\Delta$ is a parabolic set of roots, then $P$ is strongly parabolic. Furthermore, if $P$ is a proper subset of $\\Delta$, one of the three mutually exclusive alternatives holds.\n\n- [(i)] $P$ is principal and $\\delta \\not \\in \\Delta^0$;\n\n- [(ii)] $P$ is principal and $(\\Z \\setminus \\{0\\}) \\delta \\subset P$;\n\n- [(iii)] $P$ is not principal.","source_id":"arXiv:0904.0041","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"46881870e9c0b518917f965a3922d906c350dc7735a2a4fe84dbd323f1fb20b1","kind":"theorem","label":"Theorem 1","ref_key":"prop_affine","name":"","order":12,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0904.0041","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"a14448ebca79573d37a3bacc4abdcb445d514c88d4c650e891ad880c4e25d977","line":724,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:02:31+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":353,"math_hints":30}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:0904.0041","title":"Parabolic sets of roots","abstract":"We compare two combinatorial definitions of parabolic sets of roots. We show that these definitions are equivalent for simple finite dimensional Lie algebras, affine Lie algebras, and toroidal Lie algebras. In contrast, these definitions are not always equivalent for simple finite dimensional Lie superalgebras.","authors":["Ivan Dimitrov","Vyacheslav Futorny","Dimitar Grantcharov"],"year":"2009","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0904.0041","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"gg":"\\mathfrak{g}","gh":"\\mathfrak{h}","gl":"\\mathfrak{l}","gn":"\\mathfrak{n}","gp":"\\mathfrak{p}","gs":"\\mathfrak{s}","C":"\\mathbb{C}","R":"\\mathbb{R}","Z":"\\mathbb{Z}","cT":"\\mathcal{T}","vep":"\\varepsilon","Hom":"\\operatorname{Hom}","Ker":"\\operatorname{Ker}","Span":"\\